WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.729 --> 00:00:06.779
The golden age of classic Western films may
be over, but a new kind of Western has established

00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:09.599
its place in the world of prestige TV.

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:14.039
Whether you're a huge fan already or you're
just getting into it, here's everything we

00:00:14.039 --> 00:00:17.199
know so far about Yellowstone season 3.

00:00:18.199 --> 00:00:23.869
By the Yellowstone season 2 finale, Kayce
Dutton and Monica's son Tate had been kidnapped,

00:00:23.869 --> 00:00:27.849
and the Duttons were on a mission to bring
him home at any cost.

00:00:27.849 --> 00:00:32.480
They track down Teal and Malcolm Beck, knowing
that the two businessmen have something to

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:34.149
do with the disappearance.

00:00:34.149 --> 00:00:41.720
"If there's a Heaven, this is your last chance
to do something that just might get you in

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:42.220
it."

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:47.640
Teal won't confess, so Kayce makes good on
John's promise to shoot him.

00:00:47.649 --> 00:00:52.629
Malcolm is willing to give up some details,
but he suffers a few gunshot wounds and is

00:00:52.629 --> 00:00:54.370
presumably left for dead.

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:59.140
It turns out that Tate has been kidnapped
by white supremacists who were hired by the

00:00:59.140 --> 00:00:59.640
Becks.

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:04.120
By the time Kayce finds him, he's already
been beaten and traumatized.

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:08.380
But with the mystery of his abduction solved,
he can finally return home.

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:13.960
In a heartwarming moment, John's daughter
Beth reads his right-hand man Rip Wheeler

00:01:13.970 --> 00:01:18.910
a letter from John, explaining that he's leaving
Rip his father's old ranch house in exchange

00:01:18.910 --> 00:01:21.700
for saving Beth from a pair of attackers.

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:28.700
Keith Cox, Paramount Network and TV Land President
of Development and Production, says the network

00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:34.110
has grand visions for season 3 and beyond,
and he's impressed with the scripts he's read

00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:35.100
so far.

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:35.900
He told Deadline:

00:01:35.980 --> 00:01:40.720
"It's going to be great and even bigger than
Season 2; I know it, feel it.

00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:41.640
It will happen."

00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:47.260
Cox also says that the final ending for the
series is already planned, discussions about

00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:53.500
an eventual season 4 are ongoing, and the
show will ideally run for six or seven seasons

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:54.000
total.

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:59.580
Costner has made it clear that there will
be further consequences for those who threatened

00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:04.700
the Dutton family in season 2, so it looks
like karma will be coming around.

00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:09.680
Meanwhile, Beth and Rip appear to be diving
back into their rekindled romance.

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:15.140
Fans theories abound regarding Jamie's possible
past interference in their relationship, so

00:02:15.140 --> 00:02:18.799
perhaps season 3 will address some of the
rumors.

00:02:18.799 --> 00:02:22.969
But expect some big changes going from season
2 into season 3.

00:02:22.969 --> 00:02:25.440
"You can try to find a way to play it safe,
and there isn't."

00:02:25.689 --> 00:02:31.379
The cast has noted that season 3 will start
off slow, but it won't stay that way for long.

00:02:31.379 --> 00:02:34.109
"It's a slow burn, and then it heats up."

00:02:34.109 --> 00:02:39.219
Fans who are worried that the show won't feel
quite the same can rest assured that they're

00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:40.640
in for a great season.

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:43.360
"Season 3 is some of my favorite stuff so
far.

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:44.360
It's pretty shocking."

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:50.120
It looks like all of the main cast members
appear to be returning for Yellowstone season

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:50.620
3.

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:56.300
Naturally, you won't be seeing Terry Serpico
as Teal anymore, but there's still a slim

00:02:56.310 --> 00:03:01.810
chance that Neal McDonough could return as
Malcolm — remember, he didn't actually die

00:03:01.810 --> 00:03:02.660
on camera.

00:03:03.020 --> 00:03:07.460
This season, a few other recurring actors
will be bumped up to regular roles.

00:03:07.469 --> 00:03:12.930
Forrie J. Smith, who plays Dutton's cow boss
Lloyd, is officially being promoted to a series

00:03:12.930 --> 00:03:16.800
regular, along with Denim Richards, who plays
cowboy wrangler Colby.

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:21.620
It's safe to say we'll be seeing a lot more
of Lloyd and Colby in the upcoming season.

00:03:21.630 --> 00:03:26.829
Kevin Costner may be stepping behind the camera
on occasion throughout this season as well.

00:03:26.829 --> 00:03:31.129
In a recent interview with Deadline, Costner
expressed his hope that he would be able to

00:03:31.129 --> 00:03:33.360
focus on directing in the future.

00:03:34.220 --> 00:03:39.800
Josh Holloway will be appearing as Roarke
Carter, a charismatic hedge fund manager with

00:03:39.800 --> 00:03:45.100
big plans in Montana — plans that just might
involve the Dutton ranch.

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:51.120
Holloway has described his character as, quote,
"a hedge fund baller," with Costner adding:

00:03:51.129 --> 00:03:54.290
"You can't ignore him, you can't just kind
of close the gate."

00:03:54.290 --> 00:03:59.079
Deadline notes that Holloway's character will
have a "season-long" arc, so it doesn't look

00:03:59.079 --> 00:04:02.549
like he'll be sticking around for a probable
season 4.

00:04:02.549 --> 00:04:07.359
It's hinted that Carter might try to make
a move on Beth, and Kelly Reilly expressed

00:04:07.359 --> 00:04:09.779
excitement at working with Holloway.

00:04:09.779 --> 00:04:14.519
Perhaps Carter is trying to take control of
the land for himself and wants to curry favor

00:04:14.519 --> 00:04:17.010
with Beth as an "in" with the Duttons.

00:04:17.010 --> 00:04:22.540
Or maybe he'll prove to be an unlikely ally
for the Duttons in the face of another adversary.

00:04:22.540 --> 00:04:28.280
John Emmet Tracy is also slated to appear
in a recurring role as Ellis Steele, a chief

00:04:28.280 --> 00:04:31.160
litigator for Fortune 500 companies.

00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:36.060
Described as, quote, "the kind of person who
will smile as he stabs you in the back," Steele

00:04:36.070 --> 00:04:39.510
could pose a serious threat to the Dutton
ranch.

00:04:39.510 --> 00:04:45.390
Q'orianka Kilcher will be playing Angela Blue
Thunder, a Native American woman who opposes

00:04:45.390 --> 00:04:48.380
Tom Rainwater, the chief of the reservation.

00:04:48.540 --> 00:04:53.740
Angela is disgusted with the way Rainwater
has been running the casino, and she feels

00:04:53.750 --> 00:04:57.930
that he's responsible for many of the problems
on the reservation.

00:04:57.930 --> 00:05:03.840
Whether or not Angela's bold actions against
Rainwater will benefit the Duttons is unclear.

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:09.240
But considering his past intentions to acquire
their land to expand the reservation, the

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:12.800
enemy of their enemy might be their friend
in this scenario.

00:05:13.540 --> 00:05:16.180
"Working with them is a deal with the devil,
Dad."

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:19.500
"All the angels are gone, son.

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:22.200
There's only devils left."

00:05:22.780 --> 00:05:26.480
A new wrangler will be working on the Dutton
ranch in season 3.

00:05:26.480 --> 00:05:31.680
Jennifer Landon is joining the cast as Teeter,
an accomplished wrangler who may be a bit

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:34.550
rough around the edges, but always gets the
job done.

00:05:34.550 --> 00:05:37.450
It's likely she'll be working alongside Colby
and Lloyd.

00:05:37.450 --> 00:05:42.400
Teeter won't be the first female ranch hand
to work for the Duttons — after all, Avery

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:46.180
was already recruited to work there by Rip
in the first season.

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:51.560
But it does look like she'll be just the kind
of no-nonsense woman who can hold her own

00:05:51.560 --> 00:05:52.340
on the ranch.

00:05:52.520 --> 00:05:55.720
Eden Brolin will be another new addition to
the cast.

00:05:55.760 --> 00:06:00.240
She has a recurring role as Mia, a barrel
racer who strikes up a friendship with the

00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:01.510
bunkhouse guys.

00:06:01.510 --> 00:06:07.230
Brolin is most widely known for playing Charlie
in the Freeform series Beyond, in which a

00:06:07.230 --> 00:06:12.980
young man awakens from a coma to find that
he has inexplicable powers connecting him

00:06:12.980 --> 00:06:14.520
to a dark conspiracy.

00:06:14.730 --> 00:06:20.180
Her work on Yellowstone is just another sign
that she's definitely a star on the rise and

00:06:20.180 --> 00:06:22.020
one to watch in the next year.

00:06:22.370 --> 00:06:26.440
Finally, Karen Pittman is confirmed to have
a major role in season 3.

00:06:26.440 --> 00:06:30.040
She'll be playing Willa Hays, the CEO of Metro
Capital.

00:06:30.180 --> 00:06:34.500
She's well-dressed, intimidating, and never
backs down from what she wants.

00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:38.740
Now, she wants something from John Dutton
— and she's going to fight tooth and nail

00:06:38.740 --> 00:06:39.280
to get it.

00:06:39.560 --> 00:06:44.400
There's a possibility that Ellis Steele is
representing her as she tries to acquire the

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:45.040
Duttons' land.

00:06:45.120 --> 00:06:49.700
With so many new female characters coming
to the ranch, it looks like the women will

00:06:49.700 --> 00:06:50.760
be running things.

00:06:51.120 --> 00:06:56.200
Overall, it's shaping up to be an incredible
follow-up to an addictive second season.

00:06:56.210 --> 00:07:01.670
You can catch up on the first two seasons
of Dutton family drama on Amazon Prime.

00:07:01.670 --> 00:07:06.560
Season 3 of Yellowstone premieres on the Paramount
Network on June 17, 2020.

